// # hw/gpu/gpu/ — GPU Runtime Surface
//
// Logline: The GPU orchestrator, the buffer pool, streams, memory,
// classify/dispatch, and the HIP backend (dlopen / dispatch / launch).
//
// Beats:
//   1. gpu.c — orchestrator: the OoGpu type, init, probe.
//   2. gpu_pool.c — segregated VRAM pool (32 bins).
//   3. gpu_mem.c — VRAM alloc/free.
//   4. gpu_stream.c — HIP streams + events.
//   5. gpu_classify.c — kernel name + structural-marker classification.
//   6. gpu_launch.c — kernel dispatch entry point.
//   7. gpu_hip_dlopen.c — liboo_hip.so dynamic load.
//   8. gpu_hip_dispatch.c — the 7 HIP backend kernels (vec_add / sgemm / rmsnorm / attention / reduce_sum / rope / stencil_3d).
//   9. gpu_hip.c — orchestrator: bind-once + public load/unload/avail/try_launch.
//
// v3.1.0 file split: the original 1109-line gpu.c + 364-line gpu_hip.c
// were split into the gpu/ subdir (9 files). The split is functional:
// one GPU concern per file.
//
// v3.1.0 audit fix: the cap-shadow in gpu_hip_dispatch.c (a `cap=0`
// local that broke every GPU call) is fixed — oo_gpu_hip_try_launch
// now passes the real cap through to the inner launchers.
//
// ──▓▓ hw/gpu/gpu ANCHOR ──▓▓──
